And there is a deleted scene from Andy's play that, Angela, you mentioned when we broke down that episode where we learned Kevin has a sister who is actually in the play.
安迪的话剧里有一段删减片段，安吉拉，我们在剖析那一集时你提到过，我们得知凯文有一个亲妹妹其实也在话剧中。

152
00:07:30.280 --> 00:07:30.900
In the play, yeah.
在话剧里，对。

153
00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:31.980
Let's listen.
我们来听听。

154
00:07:32.600 --> 00:07:33.140
Hi.
嗨。

155
00:07:33.620 --> 00:07:34.220
Kevin.
凯文。

156
00:07:34.780 --> 00:07:35.080
Hi.
嗨。

157
00:07:35.380 --> 00:07:35.560
Hi.
嗨。

158
00:07:40.320 --> 00:07:42.840
I can't believe you came to every show.
真不敢相信你每场演出都来了。

159
00:07:42.940 --> 00:07:43.840
You're good.
你真好。

160
00:07:44.260 --> 00:07:44.960
Oh, thank you.
噢，谢谢。

161
00:07:45.140 --> 00:07:47.120
See, you never come to anything I ever do.
你看，我做什么你从来都不来。

162
00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:47.920
So what's the change?
那这次怎么改主意了？

163
00:07:48.200 --> 00:07:50.020
We need to put mom in a home.
我们得把妈妈送进疗养院了。

164
00:07:51.180 --> 00:07:54.620
So we learned a little bit there about his sister and his mom.
所以我们在那里稍微了解了他的妹妹和妈妈。

165
00:07:55.040 --> 00:07:55.420
Yeah.
对。

166
00:07:55.860 --> 00:07:57.200
But that's all there is.
但也就只有这些了。

167
00:07:57.200 --> 00:08:00.200
We only meet her through that deleted scene.
我们只能通过这段删减片段认识她。

168
00:08:00.200 --> 00:08:03.140
And it's probably why she didn't make it into the show Bible.
这也可能就是她没有被收入剧集圣经的原因。

169
00:08:03.800 --> 00:08:08.740
And listen, we do ask Brian about this in our interview coming up later in the episode.
而且听着，我们在本集稍后的访谈中确实向布莱恩问起了这件事。

170
00:08:08.740 --> 00:08:12.980
And he does share some reasons why we don't know more about Kevin's backstory.
他也分享了一些我们为什么不了解凯文背景故事的原因。

171
00:08:13.280 --> 00:08:14.340
So stay tuned.
所以敬请期待。

172
00:08:14.740 --> 00:08:16.740
Well, I love me some show Bible, lady.
噢，女士，我太爱剧集圣经了。

173
00:08:17.200 --> 00:08:18.500
It always delivers.
它总是不负期望。

174
00:08:18.860 --> 00:08:26.540
Well, I thought we can't talk about all about Kevin Malone without discussing that classic chilly cold open written by Aaron Schur.
我觉得，我们在讨论凯文·马隆时，绝对绕不开由亚伦·舒尔编剧的那个经典辣椒冷开场。

175
00:08:26.540 --> 00:08:30.780
You guys know it's the scene that kicks off Season 5, Episode Casual Friday.
你们知道的，就是拉开第五季“随性星期五”那一集序幕的场景。

176
00:08:31.420 --> 00:08:39.380
Brian once said in an interview that this scene is, quote, about an ordinary guy who doesn't do a lot well, but he does chilly well.
布莱恩曾在一次访谈中说，这个场景是“关于一个没什么特长的普通人，但他唯独做辣椒是一把好手”。

177
00:08:39.580 --> 00:08:42.020
And obviously, it doesn't succeed.
显然，最后并没有成功。

178
00:08:42.280 --> 00:08:47.200
But you hear in his voice how excited he is to be sharing this thing that he does well.
但你能从他的声音里听出，他能分享自己擅长的事是多么兴奋。

179
00:08:47.540 --> 00:08:51.240
And then Kevin, of course, says, it's probably the thing I do beSt.
然后凯文当然就说了，这可能是我最擅长的事。

180
00:08:51.740 --> 00:08:56.140
Brian said he gets asked about this scene all the time, of all the things that he's done.
布莱恩说，在他做过的一切事情中，这是他经常被问到的场景。

181
00:08:56.540 --> 00:08:57.120
On the office.
在《办公室》里。

182
00:08:57.780 --> 00:09:01.480
I mean, he wrote a whole chili cookbook.
我是说，他写了一整本辣椒食谱。

183
00:09:01.600 --> 00:09:02.720
Yes, he did.
没错，他写了。

184
00:09:03.700 --> 00:09:04.560
He did.
他确实写了。

185
00:09:04.820 --> 00:09:06.960
And, you know, I've traveled a lot with Brian.
而且，你知道的，我和布莱恩一起旅行过很多次。

186
00:09:07.140 --> 00:09:08.460
We often got paired up to travel.
我们经常被分到一起出差。

187
00:09:08.460 --> 00:09:11.520
And it is something people just really connect with him about.
这是人们真正会跟他产生共鸣的事情。

188
00:09:12.180 --> 00:09:15.280
And they have put Kevin spilling the chili.
他们把凯文洒辣椒的画面……

189
00:09:15.460 --> 00:09:17.620
I have seen it on a tattoo on someone's leg.
我曾在某人的腿上见过这个纹身。

190
00:09:17.880 --> 00:09:18.040
Same.
我也是。

191
00:09:18.040 --> 00:09:18.580
Yeah.
对。

192
00:09:19.040 --> 00:09:22.360
On T-shirts, on baby onesies, on a birthday cake.
印在T恤上、婴儿连体衣上、生日蛋糕上。

193
00:09:22.440 --> 00:09:24.240
It's just, it's very popular.
总之，它非常受欢迎。

194
00:09:24.720 --> 00:09:31.220
And I thought, you know, we can't do this episode without actually having Kevin's chili.
我想，咱们这期节目要是没有真的尝到凯文的辣椒，可就太说不过去了。

195
00:09:31.680 --> 00:09:33.540
Brian put it in his chili cookbook.
布莱恩把它收录在了他的辣椒食谱里。

196
00:09:33.700 --> 00:09:35.120
It's called Kevin's Famous Chili.
它叫凯文的著名辣椒。

197
00:09:35.400 --> 00:09:38.020
I asked Josh if he could make it last night.
我昨天让乔希做一份来着。

198
00:09:38.020 --> 00:09:38.920
And he did.
他真的做了。

199
00:09:39.200 --> 00:09:40.680
And it's really good.
而且真的很好吃。

200
00:09:41.220 --> 00:09:43.860
I mean, the way he describes it.
我是说，就按他描述的那样。

201
00:09:44.160 --> 00:09:46.260
With the onions and the things.
带着洋葱和各种材料。

202
00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:47.280
Like, yes.
就好像，是的。

203
00:09:47.660 --> 00:09:49.120
I thought we had to hear it.
我以为我们得听听看。

204
00:09:49.620 --> 00:09:54.980
At least once a year, I like to bring in some of my Kevin's Famous Chili.
至少一年一次，我喜欢带点我招牌的凯文秘制辣椒酱来。

205
00:09:54.980 --> 00:09:59.100
The trick is to undercook the onions.
诀窍在于把洋葱煮得生一点。

206
00:09:59.600 --> 00:10:03.200
Everybody is going to get to know each other in the pot.
大家要在锅里好好融合在一起。

207
00:10:03.540 --> 00:10:05.840
I'm serious about this stuff.
我是说真的。

208
00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:10.860
I'm up the night before, pressing garlic and dicing whole tomatoes.
我前一天晚上熬夜压蒜头、切整颗番茄。

209
00:10:11.220 --> 00:10:14.540
I toast my own ancho chilies.
我自己烤安乔辣椒。

210
00:10:16.740 --> 00:10:21.120
It's a recipe passed down from Malone's for generations.
这是马龙家族代代相传的秘方。

211
00:10:22.160 --> 00:10:24.780
It's probably the thing I do beSt.
这可能是我最拿手的事了。

212
00:10:26.520 --> 00:10:29.160
I mean, I'm so excited.
我是说，我太兴奋了。

213
00:10:29.360 --> 00:10:31.600
You told me that Josh was doing this.
你跟我说乔希在做这个。

214
00:10:31.720 --> 00:10:34.700
And I wrote you back and I said, this is my lunch today.
我回信跟你说，这就是我今天的午餐。

215
00:10:34.880 --> 00:10:36.100
I packed no lunch.
我什么午餐都没带。

216
00:10:36.260 --> 00:10:38.040
This is what I want to eat.
这就是我想吃的。

217
00:10:38.260 --> 00:10:39.720
Please bring this chili in.
请把这个辣椒酱带过来。

218
00:10:40.300 --> 00:10:45.300
I do want to tell you guys, we talked in such depth about this scene, how we made this scene
我确实想告诉大家，我们曾深入探讨过这个场景，我们是如何拍摄这个场景的

219
00:10:45.300 --> 00:10:47.100
in the episode Casual Friday.
在《随性星期五》那一集里。

220
00:10:47.320 --> 00:10:49.320
So if you haven't heard it, it's a great listen.
所以如果你还没听过，非常值得一听。

221
00:10:49.860 --> 00:10:50.400
It is.
确实如此。

222
00:10:50.500 --> 00:10:54.860
We got a lot of good inside scoop from Erin Schur and also from Brian.
我们从艾琳·舒尔和布莱恩那里得到了很多不错的内幕消息。

223
00:10:54.980 --> 00:10:55.320
Yeah.
是啊。

224
00:10:55.600 --> 00:10:57.200
Well, I did bring chili today.
好吧，我今天确实带了辣椒酱。

225
00:10:57.480 --> 00:11:00.720
I brought Kevin's famous chili out of Brian's cookbook.
我带了布莱恩食谱书里的凯文秘制辣椒酱。

226
00:11:00.880 --> 00:11:02.440
Seriously good chili cookbook.
非常棒的辣椒酱食谱书。

227
00:11:03.100 --> 00:11:04.220
I'm going to go heat it up.
我要去把它加热一下。

228
00:11:04.460 --> 00:11:04.780
All right.
好的。

229
00:11:04.860 --> 00:11:05.860
Well, why don't we take a break?
那我们为什么不休息一下呢？

230
00:11:05.860 --> 00:11:08.100
And when we come back, we're going to eat some chili.
等我们回来后，就要吃辣椒酱了。

231
00:11:08.380 --> 00:11:20.950
All right.
好的。

232
00:11:21.090 --> 00:11:25.330
We are back and we are eating Kevin's famous chili.
我们回来了，正在吃凯文的秘制辣椒酱。

233
00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:26.230
Thank you, Josh.
谢谢你，乔希。

234
00:11:26.610 --> 00:11:27.110
I know.
我知道。

235
00:11:27.330 --> 00:11:28.270
It's really good.
真的很好吃。

236
00:11:28.530 --> 00:11:29.250
Really good.
真的很棒。

237
00:11:29.610 --> 00:11:34.010
There's something about chili that just makes you feel cozy, doesn't it?
辣椒酱就是有一种能让人感觉温暖舒适的魔力，对吧？

238
00:11:34.270 --> 00:11:34.730
Yes.
是的。

239
00:11:35.210 --> 00:11:38.770
This has like exactly the right amount of spice for me.
对我来说，这个辣度刚刚好。

240
00:11:39.370 --> 00:11:42.290
I get a little kick, but it's not overpowering.
有一点点刺激，但又不会太冲。

241
00:11:42.710 --> 00:11:43.790
And what is this?
这是什么？

242
00:11:44.010 --> 00:11:44.890
Is this the ale?
这是艾尔啤酒吗？

243
00:11:45.270 --> 00:11:46.690
Doesn't it calls for lager, right?
食谱里要求用拉格啤酒的，对吧？

244
00:11:46.850 --> 00:11:48.270
Is that what this taste is?
这就是这个味道的来源吗？

245
00:11:48.350 --> 00:11:48.790
I don't know.
我不知道。

246
00:11:48.950 --> 00:11:49.650
I like it.
我挺喜欢的。

247
00:11:49.650 --> 00:11:51.590
The thinly diced onions really make a difference.
切得细碎的洋葱真的让口感大不一样。

248
00:11:54.190 --> 00:11:54.990
You know what?
你知道吗？

249
00:11:55.110 --> 00:11:56.910
They all got to know each other in the pot.
它们全都在锅里好好融合在一起了。

250
00:11:57.010 --> 00:11:57.590
They did.
确实如此。

251
00:11:58.050 --> 00:11:59.570
And they're making me very happy.
而且它们让我非常高兴。

252
00:12:01.950 --> 00:12:06.650
I think we should mention, Cassie, you are unable to try this chili because you're joining
我觉得我们应该提一下，卡西，你没法品尝这款辣椒，因为你今天

253
00:12:06.650 --> 00:12:07.670
us on Zoom today.
是通过 Zoom 参加我们的节目。

254
00:12:07.670 --> 00:12:08.630
I'm so sorry.
我太遗憾了。

255
00:12:09.570 --> 00:12:10.010
Yeah.
是啊。

256
00:12:10.470 --> 00:12:11.530
Is it vegetarian?
它是素食的吗？

257
00:12:11.930 --> 00:12:16.150
I was going to say, Cassie, if you were here, we would have made a vegetarian option.
我正想说，卡西，如果你在现场，我们会做一份素食版的。

258
00:12:16.370 --> 00:12:16.950
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

259
00:12:17.270 --> 00:12:17.530
That's so sweet.
太贴心了。

260
00:12:17.810 --> 00:12:19.130
It is not vegetarian.
这不是素食的。

261
00:12:19.710 --> 00:12:20.910
Kevin's recipe is not.
凯文的食谱不是。

262
00:12:21.110 --> 00:12:22.210
I would assume not.
我猜也不是。

263
00:12:22.810 --> 00:12:25.830
Well, that was incredible and very satisfying.
好吧，这太棒了，而且非常过瘾。

264
00:12:25.950 --> 00:12:27.310
And I thank Josh.
我要感谢乔什。

265
00:12:27.510 --> 00:12:30.570
And I thank Brian Baumgartner for putting that in his cookbook.
感谢布赖恩·鲍姆加特纳把它写进他的食谱里。

266
00:12:30.730 --> 00:12:31.490
And Kevin.
还有凯文。

267
00:12:31.970 --> 00:12:32.730
And Kevin.
还有凯文。

268
00:12:32.890 --> 00:12:35.110
And Aaron Schur, I guess, for writing the cold open.
我想还有阿伦·舒尔，感谢他写了冷开场。

269
00:12:35.190 --> 00:12:36.330
There's lots of people to thank.
要感谢的人可多啦。

270
00:12:37.510 --> 00:12:38.030
All right.
好了。

271
00:12:38.090 --> 00:12:39.130
Well, I'm going to put this away now.
那我现在要把这个收起来了。

272
00:12:39.610 --> 00:12:46.530
And I am going to get into, I guess, what I'm calling my deep dive area of intereSt.
接下来我要进入我所谓的“深度兴趣研究”领域。

273
00:12:46.730 --> 00:12:47.830
We each picked one.
我们每人选了一个。

274
00:12:47.830 --> 00:12:51.010
We each picked a topic about Kevin we wanted to explore.
我们每人都选了一个关于凯文的主题来探讨。

275
00:12:51.330 --> 00:12:54.770
I wanted to explore the evolution of Kevin.
我想探讨凯文的演变。

276
00:12:55.410 --> 00:12:55.970
Oh.
哦。

277
00:12:56.570 --> 00:12:58.250
There's a lot of articles about it.
有很多关于这方面的文章。

278
00:12:58.470 --> 00:13:00.330
We got a lot of fan mail about it.
我们收到了很多关于这方面的粉丝来信。

279
00:13:00.390 --> 00:13:02.170
So I was really intrigued.
所以我真的很感兴趣。

280
00:13:02.170 --> 00:13:06.590
I mean, it sounds like a very fancy title, The Evolution of Kevin.
我是说，听起来像个很高大上的名字，凯文的演变。

281
00:13:07.010 --> 00:13:07.770
Thank you.
谢谢你。

282
00:13:07.970 --> 00:13:08.610
You're welcome.
不客气。

283
00:13:08.910 --> 00:13:09.550
Thank you so much.
非常感谢。

284
00:13:10.210 --> 00:13:16.830
You know, initially, the character of Kevin was mostly used for cutaway gags or like funny
你知道，最初，凯文这个角色主要用于过渡笑话或搞笑的

285
00:13:16.830 --> 00:13:17.650
one-liners.
俏皮话。

286
00:13:17.650 --> 00:13:20.370
He was painted with a pretty broad brush.
对他的刻画比较粗线条。

287
00:13:21.270 --> 00:13:27.250
I was going through old episodes, and there's that episode from season two, Drug Testing,
我重温了旧剧集，第二季里有一集叫《药物检测》

288
00:13:27.550 --> 00:13:32.290
and it's where Dwight is questioning Kevin about the joint that was found in the parking
那是德怀特质问凯文关于停车场发现的

289
00:13:32.290 --> 00:13:32.650
lot.
大麻烟卷的事。

290
00:13:33.170 --> 00:13:38.190
I thought that this was a really good example of how the character of Kevin was used early
我认为这是一个很好的例子，说明了早期凯文这个角色

291
00:13:38.190 --> 00:13:38.530
on.
是如何被运用的。

292
00:13:38.570 --> 00:13:40.030
So I thought we could listen to it.
所以我想我们可以听听看。

293
00:13:40.150 --> 00:13:40.370
Okay.
好的。

294
00:13:40.370 --> 00:13:44.930
Let's go over some of these symptoms of marijuana use, shall we?
我们来看看吸食大麻的一些症状，好吗？

295
00:13:45.370 --> 00:13:47.870
You tell me who this sounds like.
你告诉我这听起来像谁。

296
00:13:48.450 --> 00:13:49.990
Slow moving.
行动迟缓。

297
00:13:51.370 --> 00:13:52.210
Inattentive.
注意力不集中。

298
00:13:52.990 --> 00:13:53.830
Dull.
迟钝。

299
00:13:55.250 --> 00:13:56.930
Constantly snacking.
经常吃零食。

300
00:13:57.470 --> 00:14:00.290
Shows a lack of motivation.
表现出缺乏动力。

301
00:14:03.640 --> 00:14:04.160
Hey.
嘿。

302
00:14:05.060 --> 00:14:06.160
That's it.
就是这样。

303
00:14:06.380 --> 00:14:07.980
His line is, hey.
他的台词就是，嘿。

304
00:14:08.400 --> 00:14:10.140
It's the same way he says Stacy.
这跟他喊史黛西（Stacy）的语气一模一样。

305
00:14:10.640 --> 00:14:11.120
Yeah.
是啊。

306
00:14:12.280 --> 00:14:13.720
Sorry, I'm still eating chili.
抱歉，我还在吃辣椒。

307
00:14:14.420 --> 00:14:15.060
I'm sorry.
我很抱歉。

308
00:14:15.400 --> 00:14:18.440
We were supposed to put that down, but it's hard to resiSt.
我们本来应该把它放下的，但实在很难抗拒。

309
00:14:18.860 --> 00:14:19.160
I know.
我知道。

310
00:14:19.280 --> 00:14:22.980
Also, I know there's some people who really have a hard time listening to other people
另外，我知道有些人真的很讨厌听别人

311
00:14:22.980 --> 00:14:23.960
eat or chew.
吃东西或咀嚼。

312
00:14:24.160 --> 00:14:25.180
It's like a thing.
这好像是一种怪癖。

313
00:14:25.400 --> 00:14:26.580
So many apologies.
万分抱歉。

314
00:14:26.900 --> 00:14:27.880
I'm going to stop eating now.
我这就停下来不吃了。

315
00:14:28.100 --> 00:14:28.420
Okay.
好的。

316
00:14:29.020 --> 00:14:29.900
If you can.
如果可以的话。

317
00:14:30.060 --> 00:14:30.560
I know.
我知道。

318
00:14:30.740 --> 00:14:30.980
Okay.
好啦。

